From 298a97c2501a73acb77decbca350dfc245dcf933 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:08:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: Chronik requests, WebSocket subscribers and indexer
 lag

The in-process Chronik indexer serves its own HTTP and WebSocket API, but
/metrics only saw requests proxied through the node's HTTP server, as one
"chronik" endpoint, and nothing showed whether the index kept up with the
chain.

- fullnode_chronik_requests_total{endpoint,code} and
  fullnode_chronik_request_duration_seconds{endpoint}: an axum middleware
  in chronik-http records every request with the route template axum
  matched ("" for the fallback), its status and duration, through new
  chronik-bridge FFI calls. The node maps the template to one of 24 route
  families by its first path segment (script/batch is its own), with
  not_found and other; codes are 2xx, 4xx, 5xx, other. Templates are a
  bounded set (the router's routes), never request paths.
- fullnode_chronik_ws_connections (a guard in handle_subscribe_socket)
  and fullnode_chronik_ws_subscriptions (SubscriptionLimiter's acquire
  and release), updated through the bridge.
- fullnode_chronik_indexed_height, set after each block Chronik connects
  or disconnects on its validation queue, and at startup once Chronik has
  synced; fullnode_chronik_lag_blocks, the tip height minus it at scrape
  time (only once Chronik reported a height).

chronik-http's unit tests link no C++, so its calls go through a small
metrics module that compiles to no-ops under cfg(test).

Cardinality: requests 96 series (24 x 4), duration histogram 24 label
sets, connections 1, subscriptions 1, indexed height 1, lag 1.

Hot paths: one FFI call per HTTP request (a route lookup, a counter add
and a ring push), one per WebSocket open/close and subscription change,
one gauge store per indexed block. No lock is added.

Evidence:
- metrics_tests/chronik_endpoints maps every route of the router (and
  "", unknown routes) to its family.
- Crate checks: check-crate-chronik-clippy and check-crate-chronik-test
  (65 tests) pass with RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.87.0 (without it, this
  machine's default toolchain mixes rustc versions in the shared target
  directory; unrelated to this change).
- interface_metrics_chronik.py: the indexed height reaches the tip and
  lag is 0; blockchain-info, a found and a missing block and
  chronik-info count under their endpoints and status classes, with the
  block requests timed; with indexing paused, three blocks sent over P2P
  make the lag 3, and 0 again after resume (pause and resume counted);
  a WebSocket subscribed to blocks counts one connection, one
  subscription and one ws request, both back to 0 after closing.
- chronik_ws.py and chronik_blockchain_info.py still pass.

Not tested: 5xx responses; plugin and electrum endpoints (Electrum is a
separate server and is not counted).

Coordinator integration provenance (metrics369):
Resolve Rust lib/ws insertion conflicts by preserving existing in-process module/session APIs together with authored metrics module and WS connection RAII; no backend removed.
All build/runtime/observer controls deferred by user compile-first policy; ordered source replay is not runtime approval.
